		(instances
			(project "rf-board"
				(path "/7fe63363-fb17-51fc-bbc5-b37449cf41c3/be861587-3cfa-54a5-b548-40a8e6932fd9"
					(reference "#PWR1019")
					(unit 1)
				)
			)
		)
	)
	(text "I/O expanders (D-49, D-50): U901 0x74, U902 0x75, U903 0x76 (A1 A0 = 00, 01, 10); U1001 0x77 on the bias-T sheet (D-54).\nSame addresses on unit 2,\nwhich runs on its own I2C channel from the controller. Outputs drive the coil MOSFET gates (active high, 100k pull-downs\nat each gate), so power-on, RESET and a lost bus leave every coil off. RESET = RLY_EN (active high, R3 pull-down on\nthe power sheet): no signal holds the expanders in reset and +12V_SW off. Documented exception: the datasheet asks\nfor a pull-up on RESET. Firmware: set RLY_EN high, then configure. Spare I/Os: 10k to GND in RN901 to RN903 (D-121).\nEXP_INT (open drain) signals a change on the RFDET, R1_K0_DRV and TX_ANY (PTT readback, D-53) inputs.\nU903 IO1_3 and IO1_4 are outputs: they drive R2 and R3 K0 after the TX handshake (D-63). In reset they float: the 100k gate pull-downs keep K0 off.\nBus pull-ups on this board, so unit 1 and unit 2 are the same (D-52): R901, R902 2.2k on SCL, SDA (bus about 100 pF max:\nrise 0.85 x 2.2k x 100 pF = 0.19 us, Fast-mode limit 0.3 us; sink 1.5 mA, PCA9539 IOL min 3 mA). R903 10k on EXP_INT.\nThe controller board adds no pull-ups on this bus. Unit 2: J14 takes the EXP ribbon from the unit 1 controller board (D-53).\nR904 100k pull-down on TX_ANY: defined low with J14 open (logic verification F4, D-61)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 160.02 0)
